{"title": "Teleporting Trap", "pageid": 47956, "url": "https://bg3.wiki/wiki/Teleporting_Trap", "categories": ["Environmental objects", "Traps"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><figure typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:GithTeleportTrap.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/9/9b/GithTeleportTrap.png/250px-GithTeleportTrap.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/9/9b/GithTeleportTrap.png/375px-GithTeleportTrap.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/9/9b/GithTeleportTrap.png 2x\"><img src=\"/w/images/thumb/9/9b/GithTeleportTrap.png/250px-GithTeleportTrap.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"250\" height=\"250\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/9/9b/GithTeleportTrap.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a><figcaption>A Teleport Trap on the bottom of the acid lake</figcaption></figure>\n<p>A <b>Teleporting Trap</b> is a unique type of <a href=\"/wiki/Trap\" title=\"Trap\">Trap</a> which can be encountered in the <a href=\"/wiki/Creche_Y%27llek\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Creche Y'llek\">Creche Y'llek</a> in <a href=\"/wiki/Act_One\" title=\"Act One\">Act One</a> and in some locations of <a href=\"/wiki/Act_Two\" title=\"Act Two\">Act Two</a> of the game. Also, the sigil circles in the Vaults section of the <a href=\"/wiki/Counting_House\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Counting House\">Counting House</a> in <a href=\"/wiki/Act_Three\" title=\"Act Three\">Act Three</a> have the same effect if triggering.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Involvement\">Involvement</span></h2>\n<p>A Teleporting Trap is not actually a mechanism, but a unique spell cast on the patch of the ground. They can be spotted with an <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/30px-D20.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/40px-D20.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"DC&nbsp;15 Investigation Check\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/1/13/D20.png/20px-D20.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"22\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/1/13/D20.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> DC&nbsp;15 <a href=\"/wiki/Investigation\" title=\"Investigation\">Investigation</a> <a href=\"/wiki/Ability_check\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ability check\">Check</a> (instead of <a href=\"/wiki/Perception\" title=\"Perception\">Perception</a> for regular traps). On detecting, such a trap is depicted as a several concentric lilac-glowing circles with symbols in it, much resembling the result of casting <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Glyph_of_Warding:_Thunder\" title=\"Glyph of Warding: Thunder\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/6/67/Glyph_of_Warding_Thunder_Icon.webp/25px-Glyph_of_Warding_Thunder_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/6/67/Glyph_of_Warding_Thunder_Icon.webp/38px-Glyph_of_Warding_Thunder_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/6/67/Glyph_of_Warding_Thunder_Icon.webp/50px-Glyph_of_Warding_Thunder_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Glyph of Warding: Thunder\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/6/67/Glyph_of_Warding_Thunder_Icon.webp/25px-Glyph_of_Warding_Thunder_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/6/67/Glyph_of_Warding_Thunder_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Glyph_of_Warding:_Thunder\" title=\"Glyph of Warding: Thunder\">Glyph of Warding: Thunder</a>.\n</p><p>Traps of this kind placed in the <a href=\"/wiki/Cr%C3%A8che_Y%27llek#Hatchery\" title=\"Crèche Y'llek\">Hatchery</a> of the crèche are called the <i>\"Glyphs of Teleportation\"</i> and provide the means of safety for hatching <a href=\"/wiki/Githyanki_Egg\" title=\"Githyanki Egg\">Githyanki Eggs</a>. If the player speaks with one of the Hatchery <a href=\"/wiki/Vu%27un\" title=\"Vu'un\">guards</a>, they may find out that Teleporting Traps in the Hatchery, as well as other defensive devices around like <a href=\"/wiki/Vent\" title=\"Vent\">Gas Pits</a> emitting <a href=\"/wiki/Strange_Gas\" title=\"Strange Gas\">Strange Gas</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Repulsion_Mine\" title=\"Repulsion Mine\">Repulsion Mines</a> were constructed by the Hatchery caretaker, <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon bg3wiki-round-image\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Ko%27kuu\" title=\"Ko'kuu\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/2/2f/Portrait_Ko%27kuu.png/25px-Portrait_Ko%27kuu.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/2/2f/Portrait_Ko%27kuu.png/38px-Portrait_Ko%27kuu.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/2/2f/Portrait_Ko%27kuu.png/50px-Portrait_Ko%27kuu.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Varsh Ko'kuu\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/2/2f/Portrait_Ko%27kuu.png/25px-Portrait_Ko%27kuu.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/2/2f/Portrait_Ko%27kuu.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Ko%27kuu\" title=\"Ko'kuu\">Varsh Ko'kuu</a>.\n</p><p>Once triggered, a Teleporting Trap has no harmful effect on the trespasser. Instead, it instantly teleports them onto a prerequisited point nearby. In the Crèche Y'llek, the traps move the character into one of the iron cages placed opposite the Hatchery entrance, in the plain sight of the guard. However, the cages themselves stand in the lake of <a href=\"/wiki/Acid\" title=\"Acid\">Acid</a>, which levels up to mid-shin to an average-height character. As <a href=\"/wiki/Repulsion_Mine\" title=\"Repulsion Mine\">Repulsion Mines</a>, placed all around, are designed exactly to push the possible trespasser away, the latter will most certainly touch a Teleporting Trap when landing.\n</p><p>Should the party choose to speak with <a href=\"/wiki/Ko%27kuu\" title=\"Ko'kuu\">Ko'kuu</a> and upon successfully convincing him to surrender the last egg, the Teleporting Traps around the hatchery lose their function and teleport the party members triggering them into cages no more.\n</p><p>In the <a href=\"/wiki/The_Counting_House#The_Counting_House_-_Vaults\" title=\"The Counting House\">Counting House Vaults</a>, the Teleporting Traps are called the <i>\"Glyphs of Transposition\"</i> and simply return the character to the entrance of the section, causing no harm at all.\n</p><p>Teleporting Traps, unlike all other types of traps throughout the game, cannot be clicked by the player as a distinctive object and thus <b>cannot be disarmed</b>. However, the traps in the Counting House may be deactivated by pressing two buttons inside the room.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260714234317\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.027 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 641/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 4804/4194304 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 939/4194304 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 18/200\nExpensive parser function count: 1/750\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\nExtLoops count: 0/1000\nLua time usage: 0.003/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 644504/52428800 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.632      1 -total\n 80.98%   12.659      3 Template:Icon_text\n 70.11%   10.959      7 Template:Trim\n 63.01%    9.849      1 Template:Ability_check\n 23.71%    3.707      2 Template:Icon_link\n 18.72%    2.927      1 Template:SAI\n 17.81%    2.784      1 Template:CharLink\n 12.33%    1.927      3 Template:Ifempty\n 10.02%    1.566     